/-!
# `row_residue` for q = 7 through `ZMod 17`

`vSeedPrime 7 = 17`.  Data (all checked exactly in Python, see `checks/`):
* `q7rzD r` is the lcm of the denominators of row `r` of
  `q7SourceMatrixAtZeroExplicit`; `q7rzN0 = diag(q7rzD) * M_0` and
  `q7rzAN = diag(q7rzD) * A` are integer matrices, so
  `diag(q7rzD) * M_t = q7rzN0 - t * q7rzAN`;
* for `t = 0..4`, `q7rzE * q7rzNbar_t = q7rzL_t * q7rzU_t` in `ZMod 17`, with
  `q7rzE` upper and `q7rzL_t` lower unitriangular, and `q7rzNbar_t` the residue of
  `q7rzN0 - t * q7rzAN`;
* `q7rzW` inverts the Vandermonde matrix `(tʲ)` modulo 17.

No rational determinant at `T ≠ 0`, no rational interpolation, and no 9 by 9
Leibniz expansion occurs.  Every `decide` acts on entries below 17, on one
`ℤ → ZMod 17` cast, on one 9-term dot product, or on the product of nine
small naturals.  Determinants are reached only through `Matrix.det_mul`,
`Matrix.det_of_isUpperTriangular`/`isLowerTriangular` and `RingHom.map_det`.
Exact coefficient residues: [8, 0, 8, 16, 5] = `vSeedResidueRow 7`.
-/

namespace Li2Lean.B3

noncomputable section

